    {
     "type": "application",
     "title": "Applying It: Reading the Notes on a Real Record",
     "content": "When you verify a code in the Tabular List, work through these steps based on Sections I.A.7 - I.A.12:\n\n1. **Read the punctuation.** Words in parentheses are nonessential modifiers. A colon means one of the following modifiers must be documented. Brackets in the Index flag a manifestation code.\n2. **Watch for modifier/subentry conflicts.** If they are mutually exclusive, the subentry takes precedence (I.A.7).\n3. **Decide other vs unspecified.** Detail present but no specific code = \"other.\" Detail missing = \"unspecified.\" No unspecified code = \"other specified\" may represent both (I.A.9).\n4. **Read the Includes note** under the three-character title and the **inclusion terms** under the code. Remember inclusion terms are not exhaustive (I.A.11).\n5. **Check every Excludes note** that applies to the code.\n6. **Excludes1:** Do not report both - unless the two conditions are unrelated. If unclear, query the provider.\n7. **Excludes2:** Report both when the patient has both and it is appropriate.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Verifying a Code</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Seven checks for Section I.A.7 - I.A.12</text><rect x=\"50.0\" y=\"298\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"348\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">1-2. Punctuation</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"403\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Modifiers, colons, brackets</text><rect x=\"562.0\" y=\"298\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"348\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">3. Other / unspecified</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"403\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Who lacks the detail?</text><rect x=\"50.0\" y=\"622\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"672\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">4. Includes</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"727\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Notes and inclusion terms</text><rect x=\"562.0\" y=\"622\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"672\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">5-7. Excludes</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"727\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">1: never together; 2: may be</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"763\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">together</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Applying It: Reading the Notes on a Real Record"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Key Takeaways",
     "content": "• **Brackets**: synonyms/explanations in the Tabular List; **manifestation codes** in the Index. **Parentheses**: nonessential modifiers in both. **Colon**: Tabular term needs a following modifier. **Comma**: Index; meaning depends on context.\n• Nonessential modifiers apply to subterms - **unless mutually exclusive, then the subentry takes precedence** (Enteritis: \"acute\" does not apply to \"chronic\").\n• **\"Other\"** codes: the record has detail for which no specific code exists (Index NEC). **\"Unspecified\"** codes: the record is insufficient. With no unspecified code, \"other specified\" may represent both.\n• **Includes notes** sit under three-character titles. **Inclusion terms** are not exhaustive.\n• **Excludes1** = \"NOT CODED HERE!\" - never together, **except** when the conditions are unrelated; if unclear, **query the provider**.\n• **Excludes2** = \"Not included here\" - both may be coded together when appropriate.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Key Takeaways</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Conventions II in one view</text><rect x=\"50.0\" y=\"298\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"348\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Punctuation</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"403\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">[ ] ( ) : ,</text><rect x=\"562.0\" y=\"298\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"348\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Other vs unspecified</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"403\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Classification vs record lacks</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"439\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">detail</text><rect x=\"50.0\" y=\"622\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"672\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Inclusion terms</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"727\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Not exhaustive</text><rect x=\"562.0\" y=\"622\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"672\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Excludes1 / 2</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"727\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Never together / may be</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"763\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">together</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Key Takeaways"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "Which situation is the guidelines' example of when an Excludes1 note is used?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "A congenital form versus an acquired form of the same condition",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "Two conditions that commonly occur together",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "A condition and its manifestation",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Any two conditions in the same chapter",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Section I.A.12.a states: \"An Excludes1 is used when two conditions cannot occur together, such as a congenital form versus an acquired form of the same condition.\" Conditions that can occur together match the Excludes2 description (\"a patient may have both conditions at the same time\"), not Excludes1. Etiology and manifestation pairs are handled by \"code first\" and \"use additional code\" notes (I.A.13). Being in the same chapter is not a criterion in the text.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">ICD-10-CM Official Guidelines FY 2027</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"460\" width=\"1000\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"510\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Excludes1 use</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"565\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Excludes1 is for conditions that cannot occur together.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Knowledge check: Excludes1 use"
     }
    }
