     "explanation": "Correct: Section I.B.18 uses this exact example — when a diagnosis of pneumonia has been determined but not the specific type, it is acceptable to report the appropriate unspecified code. Option A selects a specific code not supported by documentation, which the guideline calls inappropriate. Option C is for when no definitive diagnosis has been established; here pneumonia is diagnosed. Option D is not supported; each encounter is coded to the level of certainty known for that encounter, and medically unnecessary testing to get a more specific code is inappropriate.",
