    {
     "type": "application",
     "title": "Applying Lesson 15 to a Real Record",
     "content": "Use these steps when a record includes obesity, psychological pain, substance use, factitious disorder or dementia.\n\n1. **Obesity:** Follow the Alphabetic Index; the code may be in E66 or elsewhere (E88.82, O99.21). Assign an obesity class code from E66.81 only if the **provider** documents the class. If class 3 and morbid obesity are both documented, code class 3 only.\n2. **Pain with psychological factors:** \"Exclusively\" psychological → F45.41, no G89. Pain with a psychological component → F45.42 plus a G89 code.\n3. **Substances — same substance, several patterns?** Apply the hierarchy (dependence > abuse > use) and assign one code.\n4. **Remission?** Code it only if the provider documents it. Mild → abuse in remission; moderate or severe → dependence in remission.\n5. **Unspecified use?** Code only when the provider links the use to a substance related disorder or medical condition and it is reportable.\n6. **Medical condition due to a substance?** Code the medical condition per the Index plus the use/abuse/dependence code (e.g., K85.2 + F10.20, not F10.288).\n7. **Blood alcohol level?** Y90 may be added if the level is documented and the provider documented an F10 condition.\n8. **Factitious disorder:** Self → F68.1-. By proxy → F68.A on the perpetrator; T74 (confirmed) or T76 (suspected) on the victim.\n9. **Dementia:** Code etiology and provider-documented severity; unspecified if none; inpatient progression → one code for the highest level.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Lesson 15 Workflow</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Check provider documentation at every step</text><rect x=\"50.0\" y=\"160\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"284\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"210\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">1-2 Obesity, pain</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"265\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Class by provider; F45.41 vs</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"301\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">F45.42</text><rect x=\"562.0\" y=\"160\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"284\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"210\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">3-5 Substances</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"265\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Hierarchy, remission, use</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"301\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">links</text><rect x=\"50.0\" y=\"468\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"284\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"518\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">6-7 Medical, BAL</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"573\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Condition + F10 code; Y90</text><rect x=\"562.0\" y=\"468\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"284\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"518\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">8 Factitious</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"573\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">F68.1-, F68.A, T74/T76</text><rect x=\"50.0\" y=\"776\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"284\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"826\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">9 Dementia</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"881\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Provider severity; highest</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"917\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">level</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Applying Lesson 15 to a Real Record"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Key Takeaways",
     "content": "• **Obesity codes** are mainly in E66, but also in other categories such as E88.82 and O99.21 (I.C.4.b).\n• **Obesity class** (E66.81) must be documented by the provider; class 3 + morbid obesity → code class 3 only (I.C.4.b.1).\n• **F45.41** (exclusively psychological pain) is never coded with G89; **F45.42** is coded with a G89 code (I.C.5.a).\n• **Remission** is a provider judgment; mild → abuse in remission, moderate/severe → dependence in remission (I.C.5.b.1).\n• **Hierarchy** for the same substance: one code, dependence > abuse > use (I.C.5.b.2).\n• **Medical conditions due to substances** are not substance-induced disorders: code the condition plus the use/abuse/dependence code (I.C.5.b.4).\n• **Y90** needs a provider-documented F10 condition; the BAL itself need not be documented by the provider (I.C.5.b.5).\n• **Munchausen by proxy:** F68.A on the perpetrator; T74/T76 on the victim. **Dementia:** provider-documented severity, unspecified if none, highest level for inpatient progression (I.C.5.c–d).",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Lesson 15 Summary</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">The rules most likely to appear on the exam</text><rect x=\"50.0\" y=\"160\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"284\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"210\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Obesity class</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"265\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Provider documents; class 3</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"301\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">wins</text><rect x=\"562.0\" y=\"160\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"284\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"210\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">F45.41 / F45.42</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"265\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">No G89 / with G89</text><rect x=\"50.0\" y=\"468\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"284\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"518\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Substances</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"573\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">One code: dependence &gt; abuse &gt;</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"609\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">use</text><rect x=\"562.0\" y=\"468\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"284\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"518\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Medical condition</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"573\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Condition + F10.20, not</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"609\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">F10.288</text><rect x=\"50.0\" y=\"776\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"284\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"826\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">MSBP</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"881\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">F68.A perpetrator; T74/T76</text><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"917\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">victim</text><rect x=\"562.0\" y=\"776\" width=\"488.0\" height=\"284\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"826\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Dementia</text><text x=\"602.0\" y=\"881\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Highest severity during stay</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Key Takeaways"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "A provider documents cannabis use and cannabis dependence for the same patient. According to Section I.C.5.b.2, what is coded?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "Cannabis use and cannabis dependence",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Only cannabis use",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Only cannabis dependence",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "Cannabis abuse, as a compromise between the two",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Correct: only dependence. Section I.C.5.b.2 says that if both use and dependence are documented, assign only the code for dependence. Coding both is wrong because only one code should be assigned for the pattern of use. Use only is wrong because dependence is higher in the hierarchy. Abuse was not documented, and the guideline never substitutes an undocumented pattern.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">ICD-10-CM Official Guidelines FY 2027</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"460\" width=\"1000\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"510\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Substance hierarchy</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"565\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Which pattern ranks highest?</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Knowledge check: Substance hierarchy"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "A patient with acute pain has documentation of a psychological component. Which pair of codes does Section I.C.5.a direct?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "F45.42 and a code from category G89",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "F45.41 and a code from category G89",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "F45.41 only",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "A code from category G89 only",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Correct: F45.42 with a G89 code. Section I.C.5.a says F45.42, Pain disorders with related psychological factors, should be used with a code from category G89 if there is documentation of a psychological component for a patient with acute or chronic pain. F45.41 is for pain exclusively related to psychological disorders, and G89 may not be assigned with it (Excludes1), so both F45.41 options are wrong. G89 alone leaves out the documented psychological component.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">ICD-10-CM Official Guidelines FY 2027</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"460\" width=\"1000\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"510\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Pain and psychology</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"565\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Is the pain exclusively psychological?</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Knowledge check: Pain and psychology"
     }
    }
