     "explanation": "Correct: H54.3. Section I.C.7.b says that if \"blindness\" or \"low vision\" of both eyes is documented but the visual impairment category is not, assign H54.3, Unqualified visual loss, both eyes. H54.7 is for when it is not known whether one or both eyes are affected. H54.6- is for one eye, and the guideline gives a single both-eyes code instead. Category H40 is glaucoma.",
