     "explanation": "Correct: Section I.C.9.e.5 states \"Acute myocardial infarctions type 3, 4a, 4b, 4c and 5 are assigned to code I21.A9.\" I21.A1 is only for type 2. I21.B is for MI with coronary microvascular dysfunction (I.C.9.e.6). I21.9 is the default for unspecified AMI or type, but here the type is documented.",
