     "explanation": "Correct: Section I.C.9.e.6 says I21.B is assigned for \"myocardial infarction with non-obstructive coronary arteries (MINOCA) with microvascular disease,\" as well as MI with coronary microvascular disease or dysfunction. I21.A1 is for type 2 MI, I21.A9 for types 3, 4a, 4b, 4c and 5, and I25.2 for an old or healed MI.",
