     "explanation": "Section I.C.18.h says R99 is only for the very limited circumstance when a patient who has already died is brought into an emergency department or other facility and is pronounced dead upon arrival, which matches this scenario. R40.20 is for coma of unknown cause or TBI without a coma scale (I.C.18.e). R65.10 is for non-infectious SIRS without organ dysfunction (I.C.18.g). Z91.81 is for past falls with future risk (I.C.18.d).",
