    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "Exam trap: A patient had a colon resection for a disease that required surgery and is still in the healing phase after the surgery. Another patient finished treatment for a condition last year, the condition no longer exists, and he is here for a surveillance exam. Which pairing is correct per Sections I.C.21.c.7 and I.C.21.c.8?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "The healing patient gets an aftercare code; the surveillance patient gets a follow-up code",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "Both patients get aftercare codes",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Both patients get follow-up codes",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "The healing patient gets a follow-up code; the surveillance patient gets an aftercare code",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Correct: A. Section I.C.21.c.7 says aftercare codes cover situations when the initial treatment has been performed and the patient requires continued care during the healing or recovery phase. Section I.C.21.c.8 says follow-up codes explain continuing surveillance following completed treatment and imply the condition has been fully treated and no longer exists.\n\nB and C are wrong because the two situations are different. D is wrong because it reverses the definitions.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">ICD-10-CM Official Guidelines FY 2027</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"460\" width=\"1000\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"510\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Aftercare vs follow-up</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"565\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Still healing, or completely treated?</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Knowledge check: Aftercare vs follow-up"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "A patient is seen for an office visit for diabetes management, and during the same visit a screening test for another disease is performed. According to Section I.C.21.c.5, how may the screening code be used?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "It must be first-listed",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "It replaces the diabetes code",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "It cannot be coded at all",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "It may be used as an additional code because the screening was done during an office visit for other health problems",
       "correct": true
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Correct: D. Section I.C.21.c.5 says a screening code may be a first-listed code if the reason for the visit is specifically the screening exam, and may also be used as an additional code if the screening is done during an office visit for other health problems.\n\nA is wrong because the visit was not specifically for the screening. C is wrong because the guideline allows it as an additional code. B is wrong because the diabetes care was the main reason for the visit, so its code is not replaced.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">ICD-10-CM Official Guidelines FY 2027</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"460\" width=\"1000\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"510\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">Screening during another visit</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"565\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\">What was the main reason for this visit?</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Knowledge check: Screening during another visit"
     }
    }
