     "explanation": "Correct: Section II.H tells inpatient coders at short-term, acute, long-term care and psychiatric hospitals to code a \"suspected\" condition at discharge as if it existed. Section IV.H tells outpatient coders not to code diagnoses documented as \"suspected\" and to code the highest degree of certainty instead, and notes this differs from the inpatient hospital practice. So the two records are handled differently; the other options apply one rule to both settings or reverse them.",
