     "explanation": "Correct: the false statement is the chemotherapy one. Section IV.L says when the primary reason for the encounter is chemotherapy or radiation therapy, the appropriate Z code for the service is listed first and the diagnosis second. The other three are accurate: IV.I (chronic diseases may be reported as many times as treated), IV.F.2 (a code without its required 7th character is invalid), and IV.G (the first-listed diagnosis may be a symptom when a diagnosis has not been established).",
